    "title": "Tropical Cyclone Zelia Approaches Western Australia",
    "text": "• Tropical Cyclone Zelia is expected to impact the Pilbara coast of Western Australia on February 13, 2025.\n• The cyclone is forecast to reach category five status with wind bursts exceeding 300 km/h.\n• Karratha, a city with a population of 22,000, is preparing for the cyclone's impact.\n• The cyclone is predicted to cross the coast between Dampier and Gray, including Port Hedland, late on Friday.\n• Residents have been advised to take refuge as the cyclone poses a significant threat.\n• Rainfall totals of more than 500 mm are expected in some areas.\n• A cyclone warning is in effect for Wallal Downs to Dampier, including Port Hedland and Karratha.\n• Evacuation centers have been established in Karratha and South Hedland.\n• Roads near Port Hedland are closed, and regional airports are also closed.\n• Resources for evacuations have been reinforced, including a national fleet helicopter and additional flood boats.",
